## 2. Primary model (plot level, quasi-binomial, 6 classes, AgriForest folded)
n=191 invaded plots / 481 occurrences; dispersion phi=1.01; deviance 231.8/185 (null 268.6);
deviance explained 13.7%; LRT=36.7, df=5, quasi-F=7.28, **p=3.0e-06**.
Beta-binomial: rho=0.0177, LRT=35.33, df=5, **p=1.3e-06** (little extra-binomial noise at plot level).
ORs vs Croplands [95% CI]: Wetlands 5.55 [3.20, 9.63]; Seminatural-pooled 5.34 [2.80,10.20];
Coastal 5.06 [2.83, 9.05]; Riparian 2.52 [1.56, 4.09]; Urban 1.87 [1.19, 2.93].
Leave-one-habitat-out: every OR unchanged to 2 decimals; drop-Croplands refit keeps Urban OR 0.37
[0.22,0.63] and Riparian 0.50 [0.29,0.87] below Coastal.

## 3. Permutation / Monte-Carlo G-tests (B=20 000)
* 10 habitats x 3 pathways: G=77.22, df=18, MC **p=5e-05** (asymptotic 2.6e-09; 17/30 expected cells<5).
* 6 classes x 3 pathways: G=56.14, df=10, MC **p=5e-05**; 6 classes gardening vs non-gardening:
  G=36.74, df=5, MC **p=5e-05** (0/12 expected cells<5).
* Permutation of pathway counts across plots (plot-level null, habitat occurrence totals not fixed):
  G=36.74 (6 classes) and 50.62 (10 habitats), both MC p=5e-05.
Driving cells (standardised residual, MC two-sided p; Bonferroni 0.0028):
Croplands gardening −2.91 (0.0004); Wetlands gardening +2.51 (0.0023); Coastal gardening +2.03 (0.017);
Seminatural-pooled gardening +1.85 (0.024); Urban unintentional +1.39 (0.031);
**Riparian AgriForest +3.93 (0.0006)** — 13 of the 23 AgriForest occurrences are in Riparian.

## 4. Two prevalence axes (why composition ≠ intensity)
Gardening occurrences per 100 plots: Coastal 79.3, Wetlands 76.3, Urban 69.2, Riparian 57.4,
Croplands 21.7, Seminatural-pooled 4.9. Unintentional share: Croplands 0.77, Urban 0.69,
Riparian 0.50, Wetlands 0.42, Coastal 0.44.
=> Coastal/Wetlands combine high gardening intensity with gardening as the majority pathway;
Urban has similarly high gardening intensity (69/100 plots) but only a 0.30 share because
unintentional propagule pressure is the highest recorded (163/100 plots).

